  "notes": "containment.finish() records any spawn without a job in a sticky module-level _TAINTED list that makes every later precheck() contained=False for the rest of the driver run, and adds the job to _OPEN_JOBS before terminate/empty-check so a failed TerminateJobObject or QueryInformationJobObject leaves the job for precheck() to re-check (fail closed until confirmed empty). Four new fake-kernel32 test cases (create_fails, assign_fails, terminate raising, active raising, each followed by precheck) fail on 73bdbef (checked with a git archive export because worktree creation was denied) and pass now; full tests/dev_workflow: 226 passed, 5 skipped (Windows-only, PLATFORM-GATED). Docs updated. Limit, unchanged by this repair: _TAINTED and _OPEN_JOBS live in the driver process's memory only, so a no-job process that outlives the driver process is not seen by a later driver process. Real Windows job objects not exercised here.",
